
        Thanks for trying out my Micro-bRISC Device Programmer Software.
        
        You should find the following files:

        MICBRISC.EXE    Micro-bRISC Visual Basic for DOS software
                        (Non-registered, Lite-edition, freeware)

        MICBRISC.HEX    Firmware INHX8M HEX File to program into a 
                        PIC16C57-JW or PIC16C57-HS OTP
                     
        MICBRISC.INI    Run-time option for tailoring the Micro-bRISC
                        programming environment to your taste.

        MICBRISC.TXT    Preliminary Micro-bRISC User's Guide


        You can try out the Micro-bRISC software without the hardware for
        evaluation purposes. Just type MICBRISC <RETURN>. Since no hardware 
        is attached, you will get a communication error dialog box. Just,
        click the DEMO command button and you can explore the software.

        If you build the Micro-bRISC yourself, you will have a working
        PIC programmer for 4 devices! Refer to MICBRISC.TXT for software
        upgrade prices.

        The Micro-bRISC is FAST
        The Micro-bRISC is different
        Check it out!


        Thanks again,

        Ken Pergola
        (Micro-bRISC developer)

